{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"73651a459f29dd7450c6c7cc39df246c43793a49"},"timestamp":1533495163,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMDUzOTk0NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2746#issuecomment-410539944"},"message":"[GitMate.io](https://gitmate.io) thinks possibly related issues are https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/227 (datalad get  barfes), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1953 (-J support for datalad drop), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2673 (--no-drop for datalad remove), https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2369 (datalad get with ssh target), and https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2276 (datalad run  misses original files which were renamed and leaves them deleted).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1533562539,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMDcwOTkwNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2746#issuecomment-410709904"},"message":"This is indeed a result of datalad using git-annex, since git-annex itself is yielding results based on keys not paths. So, after the drop in your description an `git-annex get . --json` will return just one result.\nThere might be a way for us to figure out more precisely which paths are concerned with that key and yield less confusing results. However, I'd consider this a low-priority nice-to-have feature, which might not even be worth the effort. Whatever way we might discover to solve it might be something that doesn't really scale nicely with a reasonably big hierarchy of datasets.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"e6d4813f22ddb02ab4ff047e0d9770a56e42fd25"},"timestamp":1533574128,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxMDc3Mzc4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2746#issuecomment-410773787"},"message":"I guess that git-annex in the background actually traverses every file in a folder when performing a get (however it may do something smarter which would not require this). Nonetheless, this should not be a responsibility for Datalad as like you said, this would most probably not scale nicely with bigger datasets. Thanks for the quick reply!","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"e6d4813f22ddb02ab4ff047e0d9770a56e42fd25"},"timestamp":1533574128,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTc3MzM2Njc3Mw=="},"status":2}]}